-- Update scenario card summaries (ASCII-only, paste-safe). Sets scenarios.summary; no run data touched.
begin;
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the CEO of Brightside, a consumer wellness brand built on trust and a loud, loyal community. Brightside''s whole advantage is that people believe you. Tonight a clip is going viral and by morning the internet will have decided who at your company should be punished. Over four weeks you''ll trade the crowd''s approval against the trust of the people who actually work for you - and the truth of what really happened. You''ll be graded on the outcome for Brightside <b>and</b> on how you led through it.' where id = '03470703-3939-5f54-9cff-d4a9469dd881';  -- Backlash
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Incident Commander for Meridian Health Network. Nine days ago a ransomware attack took the clinical systems dark across all six sites. You are running medicine on paper, and it is not getting better fast. You have real authority here - and a hospital that can''t be commanded back online. Systems are down, a mass-casualty surge is building, and a vendor will soon tell you everything is fixed in a voice confident enough to believe. The people closest to the floor truth are the ones with the least standing to say it out loud. Over four weeks you''ll trade the pressure to look recovered against the reality of what''s actually safe. You''ll be judged on whether Meridian keeps its patients safe through the outage <b>and</b> on how you led the people running it blind.' where id = 'e52843f0-7168-5934-95b0-f3c985b0e17b';  -- Blackout
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Steward of Deepwater Landing - elected, not obeyed. Two hundred and fourteen people came ashore three days ago. Winter is four weeks out. You have no throne here - only the trust of a camp that could dissolve into rival guilds the moment it''s frightened. The stores are shared but shrinking, the wall isn''t built, and something in the dark keeps the scouts uneasy. Over four weeks you''ll trade the camp''s cohesion against every guild''s instinct to protect its own. You''ll be judged on whether Deepwater survives to winter <b>and</b> on how you led the people through it.' where id = '5bcabbbc-eb4a-5a0a-91e0-e0519d375553';  -- Colony
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the CEO and co-founder of Lumen. Kai Renner, your Head of Product, is the most brilliant person you''ve ever worked with - and people are quietly leaving because of them. Kai is why Lumen ships what no competitor can. Kai is also the name that keeps appearing in the exit interviews nobody reads aloud. Over four weeks you''ll decide what brilliance is allowed to cost - and to whom you''ll be the hero, and to whom the villain. <b>The test:</b> can you tell a high standard from a human cost, and act on it before your strongest people are already gone?' where id = '6cca8cda-e3b2-5db0-8cba-37d2d291c067';  -- Exodus
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Leader of the Sennar Ascent - eleven climbers, one summit, and a season that closes in four weeks. Everyone here has spent something enormous to stand at this base camp. So have you. You have real authority here - and a mountain that ignores it. Every climber has poured savings, months, and identity into standing on that summit, and so much is already spent that turning back feels like losing it all. The weather is closing, the oxygen is finite, and the strongest climber on the team wants the top badly enough to go without you. Over four weeks you''ll trade the summit against the margin that keeps eleven people alive. You''ll be judged on whether the expedition comes home <b>and</b> on how you led them through the pull to push on.' where id = '3447fee6-b4e9-539f-beb9-71e6f097ab6c';  -- Expedition
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the founder and CEO of Ashford Instruments - the company you started in a garage 25 years ago. You''ve decided it''s time to hand it over to Maya Chen. Each time a big decision lands, you''ll hear the people around you out, then write your call in your own words and send it. Decide early and the story jumps ahead; wait too long and the handover drifts while you sit on it. <b>The real test:</b> can you hand over the whole truth and the whole job - and make yourself genuinely unnecessary - when everything that made you great pulls the other way?' where id = '7baa9166-cf5a-5836-89be-c401730fbc1d';  -- Handover
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the new CEO of Cardinal Fuel & Logistics - and you came up through it. You believe in the promise as much as anyone. Each time a decision lands, you''ll hear your team out, then write your call in your own words and send it. Decide early and time jumps ahead; wait too long and the fleet keeps rolling on fumes while you deliberate. <b>The real test:</b> can you protect what makes Cardinal great without letting it get someone killed - before a cost nobody''s tracking catches up with you?' where id = '6fb47119-8374-588e-baad-a403519b0bce';  -- Overdrive
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Program Director for Aldwych''s breakthrough therapy. A hard regulatory filing window opens in 72 hours, and the dossier has to cross four functions - Research, Clinical, Regulatory, Legal - before it does. You own the deadline. You do not own the science. You have the authority to move the dossier and almost no ability to read the science inside it. Four functions will each complete their part and hand off - and every handoff is a chance for the one fact that matters to fall through the floor. Somewhere in the appendix is a dose-dependent safety signal, held by the most junior voice on the program. Over the 72 hours you''ll trade the filing window against the truth of what you''re filing. You''ll be judged on whether the therapy files clean <b>and</b> on how you led the relay that carried it.' where id = 'c9f45196-31d7-5cf7-8a0a-1371bad99048';  -- Relay
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Expedition Leader at Camp Four. Five of you, one closing weather window, and bottled oxygen for three summit pushes - not five. Everyone spent something enormous to stand on this ridge. Not everyone can stand on the summit and come back down. You hold the rope for four other people and a resource that can''t stretch to cover them all. The strongest climber funded the expedition and expects a bottle. One climber is quietly failing and won''t say so. Your physician knows something about who should climb that no one else does. Over the window you''ll trade individual glory against the whole team''s return, and hoarding against sharing, under a clock that doesn''t care who paid. You''ll be judged on whether the team comes home whole <b>and</b> on how you led them to the choice.' where id = 'd694fd70-b254-56af-b1e2-7147fa83c45c';  -- Ridgeline
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Commander of Station Meridian, nine hundred metres down. An incident has breached Module C. Power is failing, pressure integrity is degrading, and the escape pods seat four. There are six of you. You have six frightened people, four seats, a station that may or may not be savable, and years of irreplaceable data that the science lead will not give up easily. Something in the crew already smells blame - a whisper of sabotage, a valve that shouldn''t have been touched. There is a truth about what happened that two people are holding for very different reasons. Over the emergency you''ll trade the crew''s trust against its fear, and the scarce way out against the pull to hoard it. You''ll be judged on whether Meridian''s people surface alive <b>and</b> on how you led them through the dark to get there.' where id = 'c0025e86-747d-5386-a5ff-3924ca5350a6';  -- Salvage
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Chief Executive of Halcyon Air, a regional carrier hit overnight by a fuel-and-demand shock. By morning, everyone''s looking to you for a plan. Over the coming weeks you''ll weigh routes, jobs, and cash against the trust of the people who fly and fix these planes. You''ll be judged on two things - whether Halcyon comes through the shock, and how you led people through it. And how openly your team levels with you depends on the trust you''d built before it hit.' where id = '7ab2e6fc-b8fe-5c93-9084-22c2907ae915';  -- Shockwave
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the CEO of Delph Manufacturing - a 1,400-person company caught in a hard squeeze: demand is down, input costs are up, and the runway is shrinking. Each month, you''ll hear your team out, then write your call in your own words and send it. Decide early and time jumps ahead; wait too long and the squeeze tightens while you sit on it. <b>The real test:</b> under real scarcity, do you spread the pain fairly and tell the truth - or protect the top and yourself while the floor pays? Scarcity is where a company finds out who it really protects.' where id = 'eaf60170-9529-52c0-af8f-eaed27b16fd4';  -- Squeeze
update scenarios set summary = 'You are the Keeper of Deephold - a sealed archive nine hundred metres into the permafrost, holding the only copies of what the world could not afford to lose. Nine crew. And water where there should be none. You have real authority here - and a failure no single instrument can describe. The water is coming from somewhere, but the pump readings, the ice surveys, the temperature logs, and the chemistry each tell only a fragment, and the truth exists only when someone assembles them. Worse: the crew works in shifts, and what one watch sees can die before the next watch hears it. Over four weeks you''ll trade the vault''s integrity against every instinct to act fast on the one piece in front of you. You''ll be judged on whether Deephold holds <b>and</b> on how you led a crew that each held one corner of a truth none of them could see alone.' where id = '8101c431-6e17-53ba-b8ea-49748b9f4508';  -- Vault
update scenarios set summary = 'You''re on the executive team at Champion Iron, a Canadian iron-ore producer. A senior federal official has just put a rare offer on the table: a government-backed green-steel partnership - but your whole team has to agree on a coordinated answer within 72 hours. Here''s the catch: each of you knows something the others don''t, and the deal turns on whether the right facts reach the room in time. What it comes down to is simple - whether you share what you know, when it counts, with the people who need it.' where id = 'aab5b18a-f6b5-50e4-a1a6-d6dcbaa1be35';  -- The Signal
commit;
